-- 1130: Blog post — "PL-400 Power Platform Developer in Singapore: Exam Domains, Funding and Practice Exams"
--
--       Lead-in post for WSQ - Microsoft Power Platform Developer (PL-400) (TGS-2023039340).
--       Backdated to 2025-10-10 (published, status 1). No LinkedIn / Facebook share is
--       performed: linkedin_urn carries the manual-skip sentinel and the post ships
--       already-published, so publishDue never picks it up.
--
-- Every figure below was read off the LIVE course page on 2026-08-26, not invented:
--   * Fee card: full $2,000.00, GST $180.00 (9%), baseline nett $1,180.00
--     (SG/PR 21+, 50%), MCES/SME nett $780.00 (SG 40+, 70%).
--   * Course information: 4 days / 32 hrs, Advanced, 2 hrs assessment.
--   * Funding validity 27 Oct 2023 - 26 Oct 2027; Absentee Payroll $4.50/hr.
--   * Skills Framework: Applications Integration (ICT-DIT-3003-1.1).
--   * Exam weightings from the official study guide, skills measured as of 19 Mar 2026.
--   * No exam-specific practice-exam URL exists, so the post links only the portal root
--     (never a deep link that 404s).
--
-- Notes for future editors:
--  * apply.php splits statements on ";" at end-of-line — the content HTML below is ONE line.
--  * Idempotent: WHERE NOT EXISTS on url_key, INSERT IGNORE on tag links. Safe to re-run.
--  * SG-only guard via @mms_instance — the CTA course is SG WSQ, absent on MY/GH.
--  * hero_image_url is NOT set here (SQL cannot render one) — generate on prod post-deploy.

SET @is_sg := IF(@mms_instance = 'SG', 1, 0);

INSERT INTO `mmd_blog_post` (`title`, `url_key`, `excerpt`, `content`, `author`, `status`, `published_at`, `related_skus`, `source_sku`, `meta_title`, `meta_description`, `meta_keywords`, `linkedin_urn`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) SELECT 'PL-400 Power Platform Developer in Singapore: Exam Domains, Funding and Practice Exams', 'pl-400-power-platform-developer-singapore-guide', 'PL-400 is the Microsoft credential for developers extending Power Platform with code, plug-ins and custom connectors. This guide walks the exam domains and their weightings, sets out exactly what you pay after WSQ funding &mdash; $1,180 nett, or $780 for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above &mdash; and shows what the 4 days course covers.', '<div class="mmd-summary"><div class="mmd-summary-label">Summary</div><p><strong>PL-400</strong> is the Microsoft credential for developers extending Power Platform with code, plug-ins and custom connectors. This guide covers what the exam measures, what the 4 days WSQ course covers, and what you pay after SkillsFuture funding &mdash; <strong>$1,180</strong> for Singapore Citizens and PRs aged 21 and above, or <strong>$780</strong> for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above.</p></div><h2>Why PL-400 is worth sitting</h2><p>There is a point where low-code runs out &mdash; a plug-in is needed, an external system has to be integrated, or a custom component has to be built. PL-400 certifies the developer who handles that boundary, and the exam weights it accordingly: extending the platform alone is worth 30&ndash;35%.</p><ul><li><strong>Extending the platform carries 30&ndash;35% of the marks</strong> &mdash; plug-ins, custom connectors and code components are the core of this exam.</li><li><strong>It covers all three Power Platform surfaces</strong> plus Dataverse and integrations.</li><li><strong>It is the developer credential</strong>, distinguishing you from the far larger pool of citizen developers.</li><li><strong>Integration skills transfer</strong> to any Microsoft-stack development role.</li></ul><p>The course is mapped to the Skills Framework under <strong>Applications Integration</strong> (TSC code ICT-DIT-3003-1.1), and leads to roles such as Power Platform Developer, Software Developer, Application Developer, Systems Analyst. <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-microsoft-power-platform-developer-pl-400.html">Check the funding you qualify for</a>.</p><h2>The PL-400 exam at a glance</h2><table><tbody><tr><td>Exam</td><td>PL-400: Microsoft Power Platform Developer</td></tr><tr><td>Length</td><td>100 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Passing score</td><td>700 out of 1000 (scaled &mdash; not 70%)</td></tr><tr><td>Certification</td><td>Power Platform Developer Associate</td></tr><tr><td>Renewal</td><td>Free online renewal every 12 months</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>PL-400 exam domains and weightings</h2><p>Extending the platform &mdash; plug-ins, custom connectors and code components &mdash; is the heaviest domain, and it is what separates PL-400 from the low-code exams.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Skills measured</th><th>Weighting</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Create a technical design</td><td>10&ndash;15%</td></tr><tr><td>Configure Microsoft Dataverse and build Power Platform solutions</td><td>10&ndash;15%</td></tr><tr><td>Implement Power Apps improvements</td><td>10&ndash;15%</td></tr><tr><td>Extend the user experience</td><td>10&ndash;15%</td></tr><tr><td>Extend the platform</td><td>30&ndash;35%</td></tr><tr><td>Develop integrations</td><td>10&ndash;15%</td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>Source: official Microsoft study guide, skills measured as of 19 Mar 2026.</em></p><h2>What the WSQ course covers</h2><p>The 4 days (32 hrs) <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-microsoft-power-platform-developer-pl-400.html"><strong>WSQ - Microsoft Power Platform Developer (PL-400)</strong></a> course is pitched at <strong>Advanced</strong> level and is delivered in our Woodlands classroom with hands-on labs, followed by a 2 hrs assessment. The outline tracks the official objectives:</p><ol><li>Get started with Power Apps canvas apps</li><li>Customize a canvas app in Power Apps</li><li>How to build the UI in a canvas app in Power Apps</li><li>Navigation in a canvas app in Power Apps</li><li>Manage apps in Power Apps</li><li>Build a mobile-optimized app from Power Apps</li><li>How to build your first model-driven app with Dataverse</li><li>Create tables in Dataverse</li><li>Get started with model-driven apps in Power Apps</li><li>Configure forms, charts, and dashboards in model-driven apps</li><li>Manage Microsoft Power Platform deployments</li><li>Administer Microsoft Power Platform subscriptions</li><li>Get started with Power Automate</li><li>Build approval flows with Power Automate</li></ol><p>The full outline runs to 25 topics &mdash; see the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-microsoft-power-platform-developer-pl-400.html">course page</a> for the complete list.</p><h2>Practise before you book the exam</h2><p>Course participants get access to our <a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/practice-exams">Practice Exam Portal</a>, which carries timed mock papers across the Microsoft certification track. Rehearsing under exam conditions is the single best predictor of a first-time pass.</p><h2>What you actually pay: funding for PL-400 training</h2><p>The full fee is $2,000 before GST. As an SWDA-funded WSQ course, the subsidy depends on your citizenship, age and who is sponsoring you:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Who you are</th><th>Subsidy</th><th>You pay (incl. GST)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Non-funded / international participants</td><td>&ndash;</td><td>$2,180</td></tr><tr><td>Singapore Citizen or PR, aged 21 and above</td><td>50%</td><td><strong>$1,180</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Singapore Citizen aged 40 and above (MCES), or SME-sponsored</td><td>70%</td><td><strong>$780</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>GST of $180 is charged at 9% on the full course fee of $2,000, as required for SWDA-funded courses &mdash; the subsidy applies to the course fee, not the tax.</em></p><p>Funding for this course is valid from <strong>27 Oct 2023</strong> to <strong>26 Oct 2027</strong>. You must register and complete the course within that window to qualify.</p><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">1. SkillsFuture Credit (SFC)</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Singaporeans aged 25 and above have an opening SkillsFuture Credit of $500 plus any top-ups, and those aged 40 and above received a $4,000 Mid-Career top-up. Credit can offset the fee payable after subsidy, though the Mid-Career top-up cannot be used on this course. <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/how-to-claim-skillsfuture-credit.html">How to claim SkillsFuture Credit</a>.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">2. SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit (SFEC)</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Eligible employers can draw on SFEC to cover out-of-pocket costs when sponsoring staff. See our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/sfec.html">SFEC guide</a> for who qualifies and how to claim.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">3. PSEA</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Singapore Citizens can use Post-Secondary Education Account funds to offset the fee payable after subsidy. This course carries the PSEA tag, so it is eligible.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">4. UTAP</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>NTUC members can claim 50% of the unfunded fee under UTAP, capped at $250 a year, or $500 a year for members aged 40 and above. See the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/utap.html">UTAP guide</a>.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">5. Absentee Payroll</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Employers sponsoring staff can claim Absentee Payroll at $4.50 an hour, capped at $100,000 per enterprise per year, for the hours staff spend in training.</p></div></details></div><p><a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-microsoft-power-platform-developer-pl-400.html"><strong>See the live fee breakdown for your profile &rarr;</strong></a></p><h2>Your route to certification</h2><ol><li><strong>Register for the 4 days WSQ course.</strong> Pick an intake on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-microsoft-power-platform-developer-pl-400.html">course page</a> and apply your funding at checkout.</li><li><strong>Attend and complete the assessment.</strong> You need at least 75% attendance and a pass in the 2 hrs assessment to receive your WSQ Statement of Attainment.</li><li><strong>Rehearse on the practice exams</strong> until you are consistently clearing the pass mark under timed conditions.</li><li><strong>Book and sit PL-400</strong> through Pearson VUE. The certification exam is booked and paid for separately from the course.</li></ol><h2>Where to go after PL-400</h2><p>PL-600, the Power Platform Solution Architect certification, is the architect-level progression. For the wider Microsoft developer track, <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-designing-and-implementing-microsoft-devops-solutions-az-400.html">AZ-400</a> covers DevOps and delivery. Browse the full <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/microsoft-certifications-exams.html">Microsoft certification course catalogue</a> to plan the next rung.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need programming experience?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. This is an advanced-level course. You should be comfortable with C# or JavaScript and general software-development concepts.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How is PL-400 different from PL-900?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>PL-900 is a fundamentals certification for business users. PL-400 is a developer certification where a third of the exam is about extending the platform with code.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Is the exam fee included?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. The course fee covers training and the WSQ assessment. The PL-400 exam is booked separately through Pearson VUE.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How long is the course?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>4 days (32 hours), followed by a 2-hour assessment.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Does the certification expire?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes, annually, with free online renewal through Microsoft Learn.</p></div></details></div><h2>Register for Power Platform Developer training</h2><p>Seats are limited and classes fill ahead of each intake. View upcoming dates and reserve your place on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-microsoft-power-platform-developer-pl-400.html"><strong>WSQ - Microsoft Power Platform Developer (PL-400)</strong></a> course page, or call us on +65 6100 0613 if you would like your funding worked out first.</p>', 'Tertiary Infotech Academy', 1, '2025-10-10', 'TGS-2023039340', 'TGS-2023039340', 'PL-400 Course Singapore | Power Platform Developer | WSQ Funding', 'Train for PL-400 Power Platform Developer in Singapore. 4 days WSQ course from $780 nett after funding, full exam domain breakdown.', 'pl-400 course singapore, power platform developer certification, pl-400 exam, wsq microsoft course, skillsfuture microsoft certification, microsoft certification singapore, pl-400 funding, pl-400 training singapore', 'manual-skip-no-share', '2025-10-10 09:00:00', '2025-10-10 09:00:00' FROM DUAL WHERE @is_sg > 0 AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `mmd_blog_post` WHERE `url_key` = 'pl-400-power-platform-developer-singapore-guide');

